#: {{ux|en|We '''are''' not coming.}}
# {{inflection of|en|be||2|p|simple|pres}}
#: {{ux|en|Mary and John, '''are''' you listening?}}
# {{inflection of|en|be||3|p|simple|pres}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''are''' here somewhere.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|1 John|4|1|passage=BEloued, beleeue not euery ſpirit, but trie the ſpirits, whether they '''are''' of God: becauſe many falſe prophets '''are''' gone out into the woꝛld.}}
# {{lb|en|East Yorkshire|Midlands}} {{inflection of|en|be||pres}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The pronunciation /aʊɚ/ arising from confusion of "are" and "[[our]]" is rare; however, it occasionally occurs due to the fact that the latter can be elided into /ɑɹ/ in quick speech.

